From 4e058bd81ed68f9851310f8f1e7db1e5af2d4559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:15:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: x and words, not multiplication signs and
 arrows
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The panel wrote the multiplication sign in some values and the letter x in
others ("3840 × 1606 (2.39:1)", "IEC 61937, 8 × 192 kHz", "L2×3" beside
"3840x2160"), and an arrow in two ("BL 10 + EL 10 → 12", and the one before
what to do under the sentence of the heading). One form across the panel, as
the public texts of the project write it: "x" ("3840x1606 (2.39:1)",
"8 x 192 kHz", "L2x3"), and words for the arrow.

 - PictureArea() (HadesPlayerInfo.h) and the counts of the RPU's levels
   (DescribeLevels(), WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp) write "x".
 - The composer's bits: hades.dv.composebits is "BL 10 + EL 10" (or
   "BL 10") and hades.dv.composeout the bits of the result, which the skin
   says after them in words: "BL 10 + EL 10, out 12" (41893, "out",
   "salida").
 - HadesAudioSignalVar: "8 x 192 kHz".
 - The line of what to do under the heading's sentence starts with its
   words, without an arrow before them.

The notice when a video starts (DescribePlaybackMode()) keeps its own form:
it is not the panel. system/hades made again.
